WEBVTT

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.500
In order to save Pantasia from Yukino´s evil clutches,

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.020
Kazuma and the gang swore to win the
Monaco cup, and then marched into France.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:11.630
Amazing.

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.130
This brioche...

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:14.410
As expected of Kayser.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.410
These are truly...

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:17.870
the Goddess’s Hands.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.130
The results of the technique, La Main De Deesse.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:23.620
This thing’s the world level?

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.350
This Japanese representative...

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:26.630
Has the Goddess’s Hands?!

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.270
That’s right.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:30.090
Anyone can do this!

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.280
Right, Kawachi?

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.820
You show it to them, too.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:34.780
Huh?

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.120
Umm... Maybe next time.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.010
Like I could!

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.410
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.280
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.660
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.940
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:58.300
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:01.850
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.060
The critical touch and go situation!!

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.860
The prohibited Rodin strategy!

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:44.650
After reaching France,
Kazuma and the gang,

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:47.110
in order to understand the sort of bread that the French like,

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:49.890
began their training under Sophie’s guidance.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:13.380
And one month later

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.210
Everyone really worked hard this past month.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:19.260
Thank you.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.970
You taught us pretty well, too.
I compliment you.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.470
But, you know...

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.850
A whole month, and it’s already gone.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:29.850
Yeah, it feels like it happened in just a few seconds.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.600
And we finally go to Monaco tomorrow.

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:34.360
Rest well today.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:35.820
Okay!

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.110
I’ll take you up on that offer.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:40.530
“I’ll take you up on that offer,” you say?!

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:41.110
Could it be...?

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:42.700
Sophie...

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.870
y-you’re coming to Monaco, too?

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.120
What, am I a bother?

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:49.290
N-No... Well, you see...

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.120
Yes, of course that’s a bother.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:54.330
My job ends only after the competition’s over.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:55.750
T-That’s true,

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.840
but what’s going to happen
to the business at this store?

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:02.930
When our mother died and our father abandoned us,

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:06.010
my brother and I, who had
nobody, were taken in by someone.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:09.310
This store belongs to him...
to Golden Papa.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:10.390
That’s why...

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.530
neither my brother nor I could shut down the store.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:13.810
However...

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.530
In truth, after Kayser opened up
there, we haven’t had any customers.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:20.820
I’ve been living off the allowance
that my brother sends me, you know...

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:25.070
Rather than going into the red by
myself, making bread that doesn’t sell...

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:27.830
it’s better to follow you guys.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:28.660
Moreover...

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:31.330
I’ve been paid by Pantasia for
this training course, anyway.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.790
So, I have that responsibility, too.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.830
I-Is that so?

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:36.750
So, what’s with that attitude?

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:37.380
That’s not it...

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.170
Do you hate me that much?

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:42.340
Or is there a reason that I shouldn’t come along?

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:45.550
N-No... There’s no such thing...

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.410
If only I hadn’t made that promise...

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:02.190
The Ten Billion Yen Clown?!

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:03.440
Yup.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:07.660
T-That really sounds amazing,

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:10.250
but technically, how am I supposed to do that?

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:12.460
Well, you see...

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.500
At that time, I was
overpowered by the words “ten billion”

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.180
and couldn’t turn him down, but...

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:27.140
To do something like that in front of a girl who
I know, after coming all the way to Monaco...

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:29.600
I-I really should draw back...

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.850
Or is there a reason that I shouldn’t come along?

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.020
Tha... That’s right!

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:38.990
I should contact Kanmuri so we
can just come up with another idea.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:42.940
But... I’ve never made an
international phone call before...

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.370
So, how should I...?

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.200
W-What’s this sound?

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:59.080
The box that Kanmuri gave me seems to be ringing.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:07.590
W-Why’s there a cell phone...?

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:13.600
B-B-B-Bonjour?

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:17.350
Isn’t it “Bonsoir” over there right now, Kawachi-san?

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:19.100
K-Kanmuri?!

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:20.940
Are you a moron?!

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.160
If it was just a cell phone in here,
couldn’t you have just told me that earlier?!

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:25.900
I kept it a secret, thinking that

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:30.910
it’d be best if you concentrated on
your training unless it’s really important.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:34.120
If people have phones about, then
they just can’t help calling, can they?

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:37.790
Moreover, connection charges
are high for that satellite cell phone.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:39.330
Leaving that aside,

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:40.880
about the clown plan...

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:44.590
Can’t we do something about it?
I really don’t want to embarrass myself...

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.130
There has to be some other way, right?

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:49.380
Someone as smart as you
should be able to...

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:50.640
Nope, there isn’t.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:53.760
Please be sure to act just as I’ve instructed, okay?

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:56.140
Please don’t say that, Kanmuri-chan!

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:58.480
Yukino will become the president, you know...

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:01.060
All right, Kawachi-san?

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.560
Be confident.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:05.030
It’s embarrassing only because
you think of it as being a clown.

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:06.490
But, wasn’t that what you called it...?

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.240
You are Rodin.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.240
Become the Ten Billion Yen Rodin.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.490
A-A Ten Billion Yen Rodin?!

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:16.240
That has a really nice ring to it...

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:18.160
Oh, that’s right, Kawachi-san.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.960
Don’t throw away the box yet.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:23.250
There’s still an important item in it.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.140
An important item?

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:27.760
There’s a false bottom...

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:29.130
When you are lost

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.890
What’s this wrapped-up thing?
When you are lost

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:32.720
When you are lost

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:39.140
The Kingdom of Monaco

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.150
We’re here.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:48.400
That’s a really ornate building.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.650
Yeah, it’s cool.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.490
It’s an impressive building, isn’t it?

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:53.950
A really artistic building.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:58.410
This is the place that gamblers
all over the world yearn for...

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.950
and your battleground:
the Grand Casino.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:04.250
Hey, more importantly, Kuro-yan...

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:07.800
There’s an exhibition right at the
start of the Monaco Cup, right?

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:10.510
It’s true that there’s an exhibition.

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:13.220
The entire team has to make a decorative bread,

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:16.430
with which each nation will demonstrate
their skills to those who will be betting.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:18.980
Rather like the paddock-inspection of horse racing.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:22.560
Therefore, it has no direct
bearing on your winning or losing.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:24.100
I won’t tell you to take it easy,

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:25.980
but you can make whatever decorative bread you like.

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:27.480
All right...

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:30.690
So far, it’s just as Kanmuri told me.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:34.530
Hey, I have a proposal, so would you listen...?

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:37.280
It’s about the exhibition...

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:41.670
How about making Rodin’s “The Thinker”
the motif for our decorative bread...

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:43.080
What do you think?

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:45.830
Rodin’s “The Thinker”?

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:47.290
A person who sewed the button on wrong?

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.840
I guess it’s pretty difficult, eh?

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.300
I think it’s a pretty good idea.

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:54.630
If we make the skeleton
framework well with biscuit dough...

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:56.760
it’s not that difficult a pose.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:00.060
Also, that sculpture’s famous all over the world.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.430
So, anyone from any country would know of it.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:06.230
I guess for someone like you, who I
thought was largely indifferent towards art,

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:08.150
it’s an unexpected proposal.

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:09.400
Well, I suppose that it’s fine.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.070
W-Well then, its decided, I guess?

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:14.780
We have to present our work
at the exhibition in three days.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.030
So, have it done by then.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:17.570
All right!

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.410
Let’s do this.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:20.580
Right, Kuro-yan?

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.080
Why you...

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:23.040
Wait!

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:25.000
You’ve called me Kuro-yan twice there!

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.070
Oh, don’t sweat it, Kuro-yan.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:31.130
3 days later: The day of the Exhibition Match

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:35.470
That’s wonderful, everyone!

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:37.300
Of course.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:38.970
If I’m to lend a hand,
something like this...

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.480
I worked pretty hard, too, you know...

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:42.930
It’s been made really well.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.980
My sense of guilt is growing in proportion to it.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:50.480
All right, let’s go to the hall then, shall we?

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:59.320
I’m sorry, Azuma, Suwabara...

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:02.530
You worked so hard to make this bread, and yet...

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:04.040
The button is...!

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:05.790
You fool!

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:10.290
But, in the end... this is for your sakes...

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:19.230
Ouch. Ow ow ow...

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:24.410
Boy, aren’t I clumsy...?

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:25.810
I tripped!

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:29.190
What have I...?

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:32.690
We don’t have enough time now to remake it.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:35.870
W-What should we do?

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:45.370
If you’re a man of Japan, then...
atone for your sin by committing seppuku!

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.120
With that, I’ll forgive you.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.330
S-Seppuku?!

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:50.380
Harakiri!

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:51.290
Of course.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:53.340
I’ll assist you in your suicide.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:57.380
P-P-Please spare me!

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:59.380
Just wait.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:02.510
There’s no need for harakiri, is there?

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:03.980
T-That’s right...

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:08.480
Is there some other way for
a man to take responsibility?

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.100
Usually, there is... right?

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:12.810
Then, let’s have you show us,
Kawachi, shall we?

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:15.070
I was waiting for those words.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:16.820
All right.

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:17.570
I’m a man as well.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:19.200
I’ll show you.

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:21.580
The Kawachi style of taking responsibility.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:28.080
This is... okay, right, Kanmuri...?

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.080
Yes, of course!

00:11:33.340 --> 00:11:34.920
It’s perfect.

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:38.760
But... I wouldn’t be caught dead doing that.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:50.480
Ladies and gentlemen.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:54.020
We will now begin the Second Monaco Cup Exhibition.

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:23.010
I will be the host for this event.

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:25.510
My name is Pierrot Bolneze.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.020
All right, everyone.

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:32.520
Don’t be shy, don’t be shy!
Place your bets.

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:37.900
Wow...

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:39.900
There’s so many different kinds of breads...

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:41.690
Everyone’s really good...

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:44.320
I guess that’s to be expected of a world tournament.

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:48.450
They’re all artistic breads that skillful bakers
created by applying some trick.

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:50.620
We can’t let down our guard, can we...

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:55.210
Yeah, it’s true that all of the
breads here are very artistic.

00:12:58.840 --> 00:12:59.540
But...

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:05.310
within the limits of common sense.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:09.930
Isn’t this bread a little too big?

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:15.100
It’s certainly on a large scale.

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:17.980
It’s really more scary than amazing.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:24.700
After helping him, it may not be
my place to say this, but...

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:26.000
this is Japan’s shame.

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:28.740
Yeah, it’s pretty broken up, since we made it in a hurry.

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:31.700
Well, it can’t be helped, since there’s a person inside.

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:40.760
I-I wasn’t expecting it to be so hard to breathe, and...

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:44.590
When I had the flour put on me while I was naked...

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:46.930
I seem to have chilled my stomach.

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:49.640
All right.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:52.390
It’s cold!

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:53.390
Relax.
It’s cold!

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:56.810
The next step is to bake the surface with the burner.

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:58.940
I’ll warm you so much that you’ll burn.

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:00.860
You’ll have to bear it.

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:03.780
Bear it, and become the person
who made a mistake sewing the button.

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:06.780
Why do I have to do something like...?

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:10.660
I can’t watch this...

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:14.340
It’s cold..

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.920
T-This is... really bad.

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:21.400
If I were to let go in front of all these people...

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:22.170
I’d...

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:25.260
no longer be considered “The Thinker,”

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.890
but “The Endurer.”

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:40.400
This is bad... She’ll notice...

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:42.650
Leave me alone!

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:44.400
W-What happened?

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:48.030
Somehow... I felt like that bread was staring at me.

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:49.610
That can’t be it, can it?

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:51.870
No matter what it looks like,
it’s still bread.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:53.660
I guess...

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:54.700
Come, let’s go.

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:55.620
Okay.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:05.130
T-This is the Ten Billion Yen Clown Plan, right?

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:09.470
Right now, it’s been renamed the
Ten Billion Yen Rodin Plan.

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:11.130
Hmm...

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:15.810
Making a decorative bread takes time.

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:19.230
In the event it suddenly
breaks on the day of the exhibition,

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:24.610
the best that even Suwabara-san or Azuma-kun can hope to make is that unsightly thing.

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:28.280
But, as a result, the odds will go up two times.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:32.030
Since Japan lost in the preliminaries last year, and have made such a bread this year...

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:33.620
nobody will bet on them.

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:35.320
I see...

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:36.700
In other words...

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:38.660
the Ten Billion Yen Rodin Plan

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:42.920
can now be considered to be 80% successful.

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:45.340
The remaining 20% will be...

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:48.760
How can you be laughing?

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:50.340
Oh, that’s right.

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:54.340
You can see what the odds are on the live relay.

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:57.720
Right now, the odds for Japan are...

00:15:57.720 --> 00:16:00.100
138 to 1, eh?

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:04.270
I think that these odds will soon increase greatly.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:05.020
But...

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:08.860
To earn ten billion, we need the odds
to be greater than 200 to 1, don’t we?

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:10.450
That’s right.

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:13.860
Do you think that we’ll be
able to truly reach those odds?

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.200
That’s why...

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:17.380
the rest depends on Kawachi.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:20.130
And Manager...

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:23.170
you’re laughing too much.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:27.590
Mean people...

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:32.260
I-I want all of you to work a little, please.

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:36.390
If we’re talking of the odds of you ever doing
work, they’ve gone past 10,000 to 1 already.

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:38.640
All right, everyone.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:41.770
We now introduce a special guest.

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:45.730
From the proud European kingdom of Panquita,

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.780
we have Princess Anne.

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:09.130
Princess.

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:10.260
Princess Anne.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:19.180
This is bad.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:21.060
Who was that?

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:22.770
It’s cold.

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:26.150
But...

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:28.940
When will this exhibition finish?

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:33.190
It’s only 141 to 1 after three hours.

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:35.450
It’s not increasing as much as we thought it would.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:36.530
And...

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:42.000
my stomach’s condition... is in a pretty bad state.

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:45.580
If I were to let it leak out, then...

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:47.540
it might be good for the odds, but...

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:49.250
Leaving that aside...

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:51.500
As a program broadcast during meal times...

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:54.010
What will happen to its future?!

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:57.930
Hey...

00:17:57.930 --> 00:18:00.390
I wonder if Kawachi’s okay...

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:04.390
He’s been like that for three hours now.

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:10.610
I-I’m going to the toilet.

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:11.900
Do you know where it is?

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:13.110
Don’t get lost.

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:15.690
W-What did you just say?

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.700
I told him not to get lost...

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:19.700
No!

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:21.160
What Azuma said.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.200
I need to go, so I’m going to the toilet.

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:26.750
What happened?

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:29.870
This exhibit’s going to last approximately eight hours.

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:31.590
For that long a time...

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:33.390
can you endure it?

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:34.880
Your need to go...

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:42.850
Just 145 to 1...

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:44.260
It’s no good...

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:47.520
It’s no good, I tell you!

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:53.070
What’s with this bread?

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:53.900
It’s moving!

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:55.230
The bread’s moving!

00:18:58.030 --> 00:18:59.280
What’s this?!

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:01.040
Oh my god!

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:03.330
N-No!

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:04.330
What is this?!

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:05.500
This is bad!

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:07.840
We’re going to take off Kawachi! I mean, that bread!

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:11.460
We really should have just cut him up at that time...

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:12.580
No more!

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:23.390
I can’t take this anymore!

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:33.570
Princess!

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:35.320
It’s dangerous! Move back!

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:35.940
Run!

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.790
I-It’s a nightmare...

00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:44.450
No more!

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:45.370
Leave me alone!

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:46.200
Pardon me, pardon me!

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:47.060
Dammit!

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:47.580
Wait!

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:48.960
No more!

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:52.290
Move!

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:54.420
I can’t hold it in anymore!

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:58.630
Oh, you’re great Kawachi-san!

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:01.840
I thought that it’d end with the audience booing you,

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.890
but to think that you made the guest,
Princess Anne, lose consciousness...

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:06.470
I’m really in awe.

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:07.680
Don’t be in awe!

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:08.680
I...

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:11.940
I placed my future as a baker on the line there.

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:13.980
Do you understand that?!

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:15.900
Well, please don’t get so angry.

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:20.440
Thanks to you having done all
that, in the end, the odds are now...

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:25.030
over 300 to 1!

00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:27.780
You are truly the Ten Billion Yen Rodin.

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:30.160
No... fifteen billion.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:32.290
The Fifteen Billion Yen Rodin.

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:35.340
F-Fifteen billion?!

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:39.590
Well, rather than Rodin, it’s more like “dokan,” though.

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:41.300
What? What did you say?

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:45.180
Listen up, Kawachi-san.

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:46.510
It’s not over with this.

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:49.180
It gets important from here.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:50.270
Yeah, that’s right.

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:53.560
Forget about the exhibition, and do your best.

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:55.110
I’m praying for your success.

00:20:55.110 --> 00:20:56.980
Yeah. I know.

00:20:56.980 --> 00:20:58.120
All right, then.

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:04.450
In the end,
an exhibition’s just an exhibition.

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:05.950
Just watch.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:11.490
I’ll show you my true colors
as a baker in the real match.

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:22.340
They’re really depressed.

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:23.590
What do I...?

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:28.800
There’s no need to be all that down...

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:31.890
It might be a little presumptuous of me to say this,

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:36.350
but an exhibition’s more like a game, right?
Just because we were a little embarrassed...

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:38.070
Don’t be so...

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:40.770
It isn’t an issue of simply being embarrassed.

00:21:41.990 --> 00:21:43.820
Because of you, we’re...

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.320
We’re...

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:46.320
What is it?

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:47.610
Stop it, Suwabara.

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:52.660
Did something happen?

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:56.160
Actually, Kawachi...

00:21:57.290 --> 00:21:59.000
While it may have only been
an exhibition...

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:02.420
On top of seriously insulting this tournament, Japan has

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:05.920
assaulted Princess Anne,
from the Kingdom of Panquita.

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:10.260
We’ve received a severe warning from
the Management Board of the Monaco Cup.

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:12.900
We’ve also lost 2 points.

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:17.440
This is a match with 10 points in total,

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:20.650
so from the very beginning we have
no choice but to fight with only 8 points.

00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:22.530
Oh well...

00:22:22.530 --> 00:22:24.490
If we think about what we did to the Princess...

00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:26.820
it’s strange that we didn’t get disqualified.

00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:28.240
N-No way.

00:22:29.780 --> 00:22:32.490
We weren’t even late, and yet we lost points...

00:22:32.490 --> 00:22:34.250
It’s really cruel.

00:24:05.870 --> 00:24:08.300
Roulette start!

00:24:08.300 --> 00:24:11.080
I wonder what it’ll be?
I wonder what it’ll be?

00:24:11.080 --> 00:24:13.220
Turning, turning.

00:24:13.220 --> 00:24:14.720
He’s really annoying...

00:24:14.720 --> 00:24:16.300
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.300 --> 00:24:17.550
This is the world level!!

00:24:17.550 --> 00:24:19.050
The roulette that brings forth a storm!

00:24:19.050 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.640 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.100 --> 00:24:25.680
The creator of “The Thinker,”
Auguste Rodin.

00:24:25.680 --> 00:24:28.100
With beautiful creations like “The Burghers
of Calais” and “Monument to Balzac,”

00:24:28.100 --> 00:24:31.100
he has been called the “father of modern sculpture.”

00:24:31.100 --> 00:24:31.740
Okay?

00:24:32.270 --> 00:24:33.660
Really?!
